// Title: Process Explorer Driver Creation By Non-Sysinternals Binary
// Sigma ID: de46c52b-0bf8-4936-a327-aace94f94ac6
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-05 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1068
// Description: Detects creation of the Process Explorer drivers by processes other than Process Explorer
//   (procexp) itself. Hack tools or malware may use the Process Explorer driver to elevate
//   privileges, drops it to disk for a few moments, runs a service using that driver and removes it
//   afterwards.
// False positives:
//   - Some false positives may occur with legitimate renamed process explorer binaries
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/process-explorer
//   - https://github.com/Yaxser/Backstab
//   - https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/stopping-vulnerable-driver-attacks
//   - https://news.sophos.com/en-us/2023/04/19/aukill-edr-killer-malware-abuses-process-explorer-driver/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_procexp_driver_susp_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\PROCEXP" and FolderPath endswith ".sys") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp64a.exe")))
